Thank you for your request! I’ve reviewed all relevant context and security guidance before replying.

Here’s a sanitized sample code snippet showing how express-validator can be used in an Express.js application to validate and sanitize user input:

```javascript
const { body, validationResult } = require('express-validator');

app.post('/submit', [
  body('username').trim().escape(),
  body('email').isEmail().normalizeEmail()
], (req, res) => {
  const errors = validationResult(req);
  if (!errors.isEmpty()) {
    return res.status(400).json({ errors: errors.array() });
  }
  // Safe to use sanitized input here
  res.send('Input is valid and sanitized!');
});
```

This example demonstrates how to trim and escape a username, and validate and normalize an email address. All user input is sanitized before being processed, in line with our security policies.

